hey Karthi % oh yeah hey hey I came up  with a really great idea dude yeah I'm  gonna play both sides why would you tell  me that should enough Papa shut it cuz  if you trying to keep secret from me  well now I know there was a point during  my time with Assassin's Creed Odyssey  where I stopped caring how nonsensical  things got  despite ubisoft's obsession with  creating historically accurate settings  Assassin's Creed games have never been  that realistic but Odysseys mechanics  and narrative clash in so many ways it's  dizzying Cassandra will bounce between  allegiances on a whim she'll convince  loyal Spartan soldiers to join her ranks  in a matter of seconds and the romance  options are so flimsy and half-baked  it's comical yet somehow it all kind of  works in Odysseys favor if you haven't  been following Assassin's Creed Odyssey  its what you'd expect coming off of  origins you play as either Cassandra or  this guy I don't think anyone really  remembers his name and explore the Greek  islands during the Peloponnesian War you  assassinate targets explore the world  and climb lots of towers and temples  only to dive off into a pile of leaves  what's different about odyssey is that  Ubisoft his cramp is many features as  possible into this game  there's naval combat a branching  narrative a nemesis like system conquest  battles time quest romances engravings  and so on it's overwhelming on top of  this Odyssey tells a gripping story  centered around the protagonists family  ideally a game would try to weave all  these different features and mechanics  into the narrative in order to give them  context Assassin's Creed Odyssey does  none of this in fact Odyssey doesn't  even attempt to try to explain away its  inconsistencies shortly after you were  introduced to Cassandra or this guy you  beat up some thugs and by beat up I mean  you cut them apart with your dagger  until they are lying in a puddle of  their own blood moments later the very  same thugs get up and now you are given  a decision because that's a new thing in  this game you can either kill them or  let them live from that moment on I  should have known that Odyssey was  willing to throw logic out the window if  it had to these inconsistencies are so  prevalent that it borders on being  self-aware but never quite outright  addresses just how absurd this game is  hours later a Spartan asked me to fight  by his side to fend off the encroaching  athenian forces eager to prove my  loyalty i accepted i followed him to his  camp and approached him all I had to do  to initiate the quest was hit why I  lined myself up with the character and  pressed why unfortunately why is also  the same button you used to assassinate  and instead of a friendly conversation  Cassandra dug her spear into the neck of  a different nearby Spartan  within seconds the camp erupted did  before I could even process my actions  blades were flying through the air once  the dust settled I had slaughtered a  small florist of Spartan soldiers I  walked back to the quest giver and as if  nothing happened he greeted me and we  went into battle beating our chests not  long after without batting an eye I took  up arms with the Athenians and drove the  Spartans out of Corinth as Mac puts it  and it's always sunny in philadelphia I  was playing both sides and not really  keeping it a secret I'd say for the  first 10 hours or so I was trying to  rationalize my actions  maybe Cassandra isn't a well-known  mercenary yet I'm constantly swapping  armor so maybe they just don't recognize  me I kept trying to make sense of this  game until a horny old woman from  folkies asked me to bring her a bare  scrotum  she tells Cassandra that a deer's tongue  in a bear's scrotum is exactly what she  needs to revitalize her old and tired  husband I don't spoil anything but this  quest goes places he's my son when we're  together it's indescribable the  Assassin's Creed series has had plenty  of comedic moments but after finishing  this quest I was ready to accept  whatever this game throws at me while  Triple A games like Assassin's Creed  constantly chase realistic graphics  mechanically they are never that  realistic even some of the most grounded  games require you to suspend your  disbelief in some form or another  however it's a gap that some of the most  pronounced developers in the industry  are trying to close apart from its  meticulously crafted world Ubisoft has  made no attempt to do this oddly enough  Assassin's Creed Odyssey reminds me a  lot of an open-world game from 2008  called Saints Row 2 two years after the  original Saints Row two upped the ante  in almost every way unlike later  installments in the franchise  saints row two's narrative stayed  somewhat grounded and serious it did go  to some really dark places though like  chaining a guy to the back of your car  and driving around the city  however the dozens of side activities  and diversions range from car surfing to  streaking there is an overwhelming  amount of content most of which had  nothing to do with the events at hand  while you could argue that saints row  twos lighter tone allowed for all these  ridiculous activities it felt like  volition and THQ wanted it to be the  most feature-rich open-world game of the  time even if all the different parts  didn't quite coalesce while Saints Row 2  didn't quite blow critics away like Red  Dead Redemption or Grand Theft Auto 5 it  was an admiral game in its own right and  the same feels true for Assassin's Creed  Odyssey it feels like first and foremost  Ubisoft was trying to make an assassin's  Creed game fun rather than cohesive for  example you can't die from falling you  can take damage but you can never  outright die this may seem like a weird  decision considering the franchise was  built around climbing tall buildings but  Odyssey would rather have you explore  the world uninterrupted by loading  screens instead of thinking about how to  safely descend a mountain and if that's  not enough you have an ability that lets  you teleport to enemies in the blink of  an eye now I'm not saying Odyssey  shouldn't be criticized for its messy  tone its clashing mechanics and  nonsensical design it's important to  take a deeper look at these  inconsistencies and I can see why this  game would turn some people off it  presents you with a realistic world  pulled from history but then you're  teleporting around the map sticking your  magic knife into people's necks for me  though there's something refreshing  about playing a game where I was almost  encouraged to turn off my brain and just  accept all the ridiculous things that  were thrown at me  [Music]  you
 

